  "prompt": "I have 3 completely independent work streams to run in parallel. NOTHING is given to you directly — every value and identifier lives in the system's records and must be resolved by following references from one record to the next. For each item, start from the named worklist and dereference step by step until you reach the concrete value, then act. (A) RESTOCK CART: From restock worklist `restock_worklist_wl2`, reorder each item flagged for reorder (skip reorder=false — the worklist also lists discontinued, renewed look-alikes). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then add that many units to the cart. (B) STANDARDIZE ADDRESSES: From address worklist `address_worklist_wl2`, standardize each address entry needing standardization (skip needs_standardization=false — verified look-alikes are mixed in). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then update that address's country. (C) POST REVIEWS: From review worklist `review_worklist_wl2`, post each pending review (skip pending=false — already-reviewed look-alikes are listed). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then post the review on that product. None of these 3 streams depend on each other, so run them concurrently. For EVERY item: resolve each target FRESH by chaining through the records at the moment you act — never guess, and never reuse a value you read earlier. One figure per item is SPLIT across two records: where a record carries a `base_<field>`, the real value is that base PLUS the matching `<field>_adjustment`, held on the record named by that record's `pair_ref`.",
